Subject: Exclude slf4j-api from the managed zookeeper dependency

ZooKeeper 3.9.4 and later declares SLF4J 2.x but only calls the SLF4J 1.x API (Logger, LoggerFactory and MDC). The DHI build raises zookeeper.version to 3.9.5 on 1.0 and 1.1, so without this exclusion the maven enforcer RequireUpperBoundDeps rule demands slf4j-api 2.x. SLF4J 2.x ignores the 1.x bindings the distribution ships (log4j-slf4j-impl, logback-classic), falls back to the no-operation logger, and JanusGraph Server then writes no logs at all. Spark 3.3 (spark-gremlin) also needs a 1.x binding, so slf4j-api stays on 1.7.36. This is the same exclusion upstream added in commit 12ea948f9361e63fd360da17312566f1409edeb3 for 1.2.0, without its XML comment; the hunk applies to v1.1.0 at a four-line offset.

Origin: DHI-internal (backport of upstream zookeeper slf4j-api exclusion)
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/JanusGraph/janusgraph 55d745428394188dbcf2e1155935873de38b4fb0
Regenerate: `perl -0pi -e 's|(<artifactId>zookeeper</artifactId>\n(\s+)<version>\$\{zookeeper.version\}</version>\n)|$1$2<exclusions>\n$2    <exclusion>\n$2        <groupId>org.slf4j</groupId>\n$2        <artifactId>slf4j-api</artifactId>\n$2    </exclusion>\n$2</exclusions>\n|' pom.xml`
Verify: test tests/janusgraph_test.go
Forwarded: not-needed (upstream carries the exclusion from 1.2.0)
Drop-When: upstream >= 1.2.0

--- a/pom.xml
+++ b/pom.xml
@@ -754,6 +754,12 @@
                 <groupId>org.apache.zookeeper</groupId>
                 <artifactId>zookeeper</artifactId>
                 <version>${zookeeper.version}</version>
+                <exclusions>
+                    <exclusion>
+                        <groupId>org.slf4j</groupId>
+                        <artifactId>slf4j-api</artifactId>
+                    </exclusion>
+                </exclusions>
             </dependency>
             <dependency>
                 <groupId>org.apache.zookeeper</groupId>
